## 2. The main create pipeline (all ordered side-effects and gates)

The real work is in the private `createOwner(...)` (lines 190–225). This is the single ordered list of validations and side-effects:

```java
190      private ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> createOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
191          Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
192          if (!normalizeAndValidateFields(owner)) {
193              return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
194          }
195          LocalDate suppliedRegistrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
196          if (suppliedRegistrationDate != null && suppliedRegistrationDate.isAfter(LocalDate.now())) {
197              return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
198          }
199          LocalDate registrationDate = resolveRegistrationDate(suppliedRegistrationDate);
200          owner.setRegistrationDate(registrationDate);
201          if (countOwnersRegisteredOn(registrationDate) >= 100) {
202              return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS);
203          }
204          owner.setHouseholdId(householdId(owner));
205          owner.setIdentityKey(identityKey(owner));
206          if (isDuplicate(owner)) {
207              return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
208          }
209          boolean sharesHousehold = Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold());
210          if (!sharesHousehold && hasExistingHousehold(owner)) {
211              return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
212          }
213          if (countOwnersInCity(owner.getCity()) >= 50) {
214              return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);
215          }
216          assignRegistrationAttributes(owner, sharesHousehold);
217          this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
218          AUDIT.info("Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}",
219              owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), owner.getMembershipLevel(),
220              owner.getMembershipNumber());
221          HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
222          headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
223              .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
224          return new ResponseEntity<>(buildOwnerDto(owner), headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
225      }
```

The ordered effects/gates, with the helper methods that implement them (all in the same file):

- **Map DTO → entity** (line 191) via `ownerMapper.toOwner(...)`.
- **Normalize + validate fields** `normalizeAndValidateFields` (lines 235–258): normalizes address (`normalizeAddressFields`, 272–287, composes flat `address` from `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, upper-cases, expands ST/RD/AVE abbreviations); lower-cases/trims email and checks `EMAIL_PATTERN` (line 85) and disposable-domain blocklist `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` (lines 88–89, check at 294–300); postcode-for-city check `isPostcodeValidForCity` (426–440); telephone normalization to E.164 `normalizeTelephone` (453–469) with national-length check (476–482). Any failure → **400**.
- **Future registration date** → **400** (196–198).
- **Resolve registration date** `resolveRegistrationDate` (612–615) rolling forward past weekends/holidays `toBusinessDay` (633–639), `PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` (621–626); mutates `owner.setRegistrationDate` (200).
- **Per-day cap** ≥100 → **429** (`countOwnersRegisteredOn`, 683–687).
- **Set `householdId`** (204, `householdId` 788–792, SHA-256) and **`identityKey`** (205, 697–702).
- **Duplicate identity gate** `isDuplicate` (710–717) → **409**.
- **Household gate** `hasExistingHousehold`/`findHousemates` (516–518, 764–770), bypassed by `sharesHousehold` → **409** (210–212).
- **Per-city cap** ≥50 → **409** (`countOwnersInCity`, 598–603).
- **Assign derived attributes** `assignRegistrationAttributes` (495–507): sets `customerCode` (`generateCustomerCode`+`deduplicateCustomerCode` 566–592, SHA-256 hash + collision suffix), `membershipNumber` (`generateMembershipNumber` 646–648), `householdId` again, `namesakeCount` (`countNamesakes` 664–671), `householdMemberCount` (`countHouseholdMembers` 776–778), and possible-duplicate flags (`assignPossibleDuplicate`/`findPossibleDuplicateOf` 527–555).
- **Persist**: `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` (217).
- **Audit log** to the dedicated `AUDIT` logger (72, 218–220).
- **Set `Location` header** and return **201 CREATED** with body from `buildOwnerDto` (308–312), which also computes the per-response `bulkSignupWarning` flag (`isBulkSignupWarning` 678–680).

Note the many read helpers call `clinicService.findAllOwners()` — each triggers a read transaction.

---

## 3. The request DTO and all its Bean Validation annotations

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/target/generated-sources/openapi/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/dto/OwnerFieldsDto.java`** — this is the `@Valid @RequestBody` type. Validation annotations are on the getters (declared-order-independent; Bean Validation runs them all):

- `title` (line 81): `@Size(max = 10)`
- `firstName` (line 102): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
- `lastName` (line 123): `@NotNull @Pattern(regexp = "^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$") @Size(min = 1, max = 30)`
