- `city` (line 52): `@NotEmpty`
- `postcode` (line 56): `@Pattern(regexp = "^[0-9]{4}$", message = "Postcode must be 4 digits")`
- `telephone` (lines 60–61): `@NotEmpty @Pattern(regexp = "^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$", message = "Phone number must be in E.164 form")`
- `email`, `title`, `addressLine1/2`, `registrationDate`, `birthDate`, and all derived/persisted columns (`customerCode`, `householdId`, `identityKey`, `namesakeCount`, `householdMemberCount`, `membershipNumber`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`, `deleted`): no constraints.
- `pets` (line 100): `@OneToMany(cascade = CascadeType.ALL, mappedBy = "owner", fetch = FetchType.EAGER)` — a save cascades to pets, but the create path never attaches pets.

**Superclass `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`**: `firstName` (line 32) and `lastName` (line 36) each `@NotEmpty`.

Many `@Transient` derived getters (salutation, membershipPoints/level, fiscalYear, contactPreference, ageBand, checkDigit, region, locality, timezone, telephoneDisplay) are computed on read and are not persisted or validated.

---

## 5. Custom validators / @Validated groups / @InitBinder

- **None on the owner path.** There is no `@InitBinder` or `WebDataBinder` anywhere in `src/main`. No validation groups are used.
- The only `ConstraintValidator` in the codebase is `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/validation/PetAgeValidator.java` (`ConstraintValidator<PetAgeValidation, LocalDate>`), which validates **pet** birth dates — it is not referenced by any Owner DTO/entity, so it does not run for `POST /api/owners`.
- `@Validated` appears only on the generated `OwnersApi` interface (enabling method-parameter validation of `@Valid @RequestBody`).

---

## 6. Global exception handling relevant to this endpoint

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** — `@ControllerAdvice` (line 48). Relevant handlers:

- `handleMethodArgumentNotValidException` (lines 133–154): converts the `@Valid` failure on `OwnerFieldsDto` into **400** with a `ProblemDetail` containing `errors` (field names) and `schemaValidationErrors` (built by `toValidationMessage`, 163–174).
- `handleAccessDeniedException` (lines 84–87): re-throws so Spring Security produces **403** for the failed `@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")`.
- `handleDataIntegrityViolationException` (lines 113–124): maps DB constraint violations to **404**.
- `handleGeneralException` (lines 96–103): any other exception → **500**.

No custom servlet filters/interceptors touch this endpoint beyond Spring Security's method-security enforcement of the `@PreAuthorize` role.

---

## 7. Transaction boundaries

- The controller `addOwner`/`createOwner` methods are **not** `@Transactional` — there is no single transaction wrapping the whole create pipeline. Each service call runs in its own transaction.
- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`**:
  - `saveOwner` (lines 233–237): `@Transactional`, calls `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. This is the only write transaction on the create path; the actual Hibernate INSERT/flush (and thus entity-level constraint validation) happens here.
  - `findAllOwners` (127–129), `findOwnerById` (202–204): `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` — invoked repeatedly by the duplicate/household/namesake/city-count helpers, each in its own read-only transaction.
- **`OwnerRepository`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`) is a plain interface with a standard `save(Owner)`; there is no custom persistence logic or lifecycle hook there.

**No `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners` exist on `Owner`, `Person`, or `BaseEntity`** — every default and derived value is set explicitly in the controller before `saveOwner`, not via JPA lifecycle callbacks.

