- **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`**:
  - `saveOwner` (lines 233–237): `@Transactional`, calls `ownerRepository.save(owner)`. This is the only write transaction on the create path; the actual Hibernate INSERT/flush (and thus entity-level constraint validation) happens here.
  - `findAllOwners` (127–129), `findOwnerById` (202–204): `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` — invoked repeatedly by the duplicate/household/namesake/city-count helpers, each in its own read-only transaction.
- **`OwnerRepository`** (`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`) is a plain interface with a standard `save(Owner)`; there is no custom persistence logic or lifecycle hook there.

**No `@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners` exist on `Owner`, `Person`, or `BaseEntity`** — every default and derived value is set explicitly in the controller before `saveOwner`, not via JPA lifecycle callbacks.
